+An optional frequency-shaped cost adds a filtered applied-common-brake state
+to the controller (not the observer). Its exact discrete decay comes from the
+generator's time constant. Engagement initializes it from prior applied brake
+and includes its feedback in output matching. A zero memory weight recovers
+the original 19-state gain; positive weights penalize persistent brake use.
+The speed integrator can still demand sustained brake, particularly with a
+biased synthetic airspeed estimate: this penalty does not fix estimation bias.
+SITL-only diagnostic output can be enabled at generation time and is disabled
+in the normal generated header. No flight parameter indices are changed.
+Local unconstrained poles do not establish stability with this one-sided authority.
+This is a three-input design, not the archived two-input scheduled LQI.
 
 Model-derived equilibrium feed-forward covers turn, climb and airspeed demands.
 The local reference governor limits climb to +/-0.5 m/s, heading rate to +/-10
